  "description": "A curse is laid in a crypt. 0 to 900 ms: a whisper that is sucked backwards into the caster's mouth (breathy syllables recorded forwards, played in reverse, so each one swells and stops dead). 900 ms: the curse lands. A huge throat, something far bigger than a person, lets out a falling growl from 'ah' down to a closed 'oo', its pitch sinking a fifth over 1.2 s, ring-modulated at 41 Hz so it rattles. Over it a cracked iron bell tolls once, a little flat. The crypt keeps both for three seconds.",
